NEARS-3521 AC6 — :amount placeholder fix, live evidence

Trigger: customer@nears.com added a below-minimum item (Organic Spinach, item 13, $4.00) to
cart for store 3 "Organic Paradise" (minimum_order = 10.00 AED), then called
POST /api/v1/customer/order/place (non-prescription — the gate is skipped for prescription
orders per `!$is_prescription` in OrderPlacementService::placeOrderTransaction).

English (default, no X-localization header):
  HTTP 406 {"errors":[{"code":"order_time","message":"You need to order at least 10 AED"}]}
  -> real numeric amount (10), currency code appended, no literal ":amount", not blank, not
  doubled.

Arabic (X-localization: ar header, accepted — zero localization_header_rejected log lines):
  HTTP 406 {"errors":[{"code":"order_time","message":"You need to order at least 10 AED"}]}
  -> same numeric interpolation succeeded under App::setLocale('ar'). The literal message
  text is identical to English because resources/lang/ar/messages.php's
  'you_need_to_order_at_least' key is itself an untranslated English-language placeholder
  string (confirmed by reading the file — this is a pre-existing i18n-completeness gap in
  the ar lang file, NOT something NEARS-3521 introduced or is in scope to fix; both ar and en
  messages.php were touched identically by this ticket's diff, i.e. the :amount fix was
  applied symmetrically). Filed as a followups[] note.
